 and the  right tone and the right  heart and um  they all said yes we went to each of  them and showed them designs and  drawings and then the easter bunny kind  of you know we knew hugh was going to be  involved and uh  i guess it kind of came about us  thinking about what the character of the  bunny was going to be that it was going  to be a little more of like a cowboy  kind of tracker kind of ornery kind of a  guy and i guess we ended up like  actually listening to the australian  accent from australia where he had  played a character that was very close  to what bunny was going to be and it  just felt like well that fit yeah let's  just have to do that you know and  there's a series of 13 books that are  being released i think about six are out  right now  and so he was as he was writing the  mythologies in the deep deep background  for all the characters we were  developing the movie but  he's been incredibly involved for the  last four years and he's so happy and  thrilled with how it how it turned out  it's you know a labor of love for him  and for us but it was a great  collaboration they kind of complement  each other more than one is based on the  other so it worked really well actually  you know we were showing him all of our  artwork and he'd chime in and you know  he and i would talk about movie  references yeah and the designs are all  based on his early early designs that he  had been carrying around him for 20  years so they're very closely integrated  guillermo who's like you know he's a lot  like north in the movie you know he's a  big guy really excited and passionate  and full of energy and and and he was  like the greatest cheerleader and the  greatest support and you know shoulder  to cry on and uh was always there to  make sure that we were you know staying  passionate about the things we had been  passionate about in the first place and  uh not let go of the uh  the uh the great stuff i mean and all  the stuff that meant something to him  t